# A power chain put up BY HAND and a piece run off it (docs/VISION.md §9), which
# nothing proved before: `tours/defences.tour` and `tours/turret.tour` both open
# with `--holding=...,wind_spinner,battery_stack,...`, so every frame in the
# repository showing a powered holding is a frame of a holding the boot option
# stood up. The claim "build shelters/towns, POWER, food, defence" had its power
# half staged, and the half nobody walked held a real bug: a spinner read the
# wind SIGNED, so it made nothing every time the air came from the other quarter.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/power.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=timber:4,scrap:8,iron:2,copper:3,deadwood:4,stone:4
#
# (--give is exactly the four pieces' costs — a spinner is timber 1, plate 2 and
# iron 1; a stack plate 3 and copper 1; a mast timber 1, plate 1 and copper 1;
# a hearth stone 3 and dead wood 2 — all of it takeable off the coast by hand.
# The taking is survival's proof, not this one's.)
#
# The eight world hours in the middle are not padding. A bank starts empty, a
# spinner makes 2.0 against the mast's 0.6, and the wind on a clear day comes and
# goes on a 37-minute swing — so a yard wired one minute is dark the next until
# the stack has something in it. That is the whole reason the piece exists, and
# it is why the frame that claims `powered` is taken after the hours and not
# before: the first run of this tour held `powered` at 13 s and had lost it by
# 15 s, which is what turned up the signed-wind bug.
coast calm
place spawn
wait 0.4
# Out of the village square to open ground, on the real keys.
walk -1,1 1.5
wait 0.5
shot 01-somewhere-to-put-it with land:coast
# The spinner first, because it is the only thing here that MAKES anything, and
# the only generator anybody can build at all: SOLAR_ARRAY and PEDAL_DYNAMO are
# named in StructureKind and have no row. It founds the holding.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.6
shot 02-the-slate-asks-what-to-put-up with app:holding
choose build_wind_spinner
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.5
shot 03-something-that-makes-power with app:holding, piece:wind_spinner
# A stack to hold what the wind made, so the mast does not go off every time the
# air drops. Power is a RATE and charge is an AMOUNT, and this is the amount.
choose build_battery_stack
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.4
# And the thing that spends it. A mast draws 0.6 and gives the place away on the
# loudest channel there is, which is the whole bargain: power buys reach and
# reach is what a machine hears.
choose build_radio_mast
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.4
# A hearth, so the yard is somewhere a person lives and not an installation.
choose build_hearth
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.4
tap pause
wait 0.6
# Eight world hours. The holding settles up from its own timestamp in half-hour
# slices: the wind turns the blades, the surplus goes into the stack, and by the
# far end the mast is up whether it is blowing at that exact minute or not.
hour 18
wait 1.6
await powered 8
shot 04-a-yard-with-power-in-it with holding, powered, piece:wind_spinner, piece:battery_stack
# What it cost: the slate's bars now carry a power channel nobody staged.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.6
shot 05-what-a-machine-hears-of-it with app:holding, powered, piece:radio_mast
tap pause
wait 0.8
